[00:00.00] What a dream I had, pressed in work and deed, Clothed in criminal hand of smoky burgundy.
[00:28.00] Softer than the rain, I wandered empty streets down past the shop displays.
[00:39.00] I heard cathedral bells dripping down the alleyways as I walked on.
[00:51.00] And when you ran to me, your cheeks flushed with the night.
[00:57.00] We walked on frosted fields of tuniper and lamp-line, I held your hand.
[01:28.00] And when I walked and felt you warm in here, I kissed your honey hair with my grateful tears.
[01:41.00] Oh I love you girl, oh I love you.
